<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine Airlines signs pact with labour union.</title>
<headline>Philippine Airlines signs pact with labour union.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippines Airlines Inc said on Monday it had signed an accord with its third labour union, the PAL Employees Association (PALEA), which should put an end to its labour problems.</p>
<p>An official said this should clear the way for the airline to focus on its refleeting programme and on improving its operations.</p>
<p>PALEA is composed of about 8,000 to 9,000 ground crew and other employees. They had threatened to strike last month on Christmas Day.</p>
<p>In recent months, the airline management had also settled with the 2,000-member stewards' union and 615-member pilots' association.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom 63 2 841-8937 fax 8176267</p>
